{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/211700-pseshkf-question","id":211700,"title":"Pseshkf Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-28T15:22:44-07:00","id":211700,"title":"Pseshkf Question","content":"<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Weapons so coated cause 1 additional lethal damage to physical targets (including Kindred)&quot;<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the rest of the damage for a normal weapon is also converted to lethal against kindred? If I used a knife and coated it, would all the damage I do with that knife then be considered supernatural and be lethal to Kindred? My Storyteller and I are having a bit of a disagreement about it at the moment, since he thinks it would only do that 1 lethal to kindred and the rest would be bashing.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:27:48-07:00","id":211718,"title":"","content":"I believe your ST is correct, since it's mechanically similar to the Kindred Dueling style merit, which only convert's the weapon's damage modifier to Lethal against Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T15:30:34-07:00","id":211723,"title":"","content":"Your ST is always right.<br /> <br /> Facetiousness aside, I'd read as 1 additional point of lethal damage (no conversion). The &quot;familiar with the system&quot; and gamer part of me thinks that an attack doing different types of damage at the same time &quot;feels&quot; weird as a mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T00:03:30-07:00","id":212205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/211700-pseshkf-question?p=211723#post211723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your ST is always right.<br /> <br /> Facetiousness aside, I'd read as 1 additional point of lethal damage (no conversion). <b>The &quot;familiar with the system&quot; and gamer part of me thinks that an attack doing different types of damage at the same time &quot;feels&quot; weird as a mechanic.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>But that was done in Kindred Dueling, so this thing has a precedent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T01:45:36-07:00","id":212229,"title":"","content":"Two types of damage really isn't different than armor reducing all damage and then you receive one bashing. Think of it this way, all the weapon damage from the weapon as normal is reduced away for noncorporeals. The weapon does what it does and Psheshkf tacks on a bonus. I think it is safe to say it doesn't convert damage because that would likely be a power with a higher cost, vitae or experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T14:12:38-07:00","id":212773,"title":"","content":"Yeah, only 1 lethal damage. It's already very powerful. Any hits you cause will require at least 1,5 vitae to heal as a minimum, while normally it'd be 0.5. It is quite potent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T18:45:53-07:00","id":486947,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Pseshkf is a pretty neat power in its own right and already deals different bonuses of damage to different creatures.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T17:27:40-07:00","id":487809,"title":"","content":"It should just add one lethal to Kindred, not convert the whole of the weapon damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T20:42:52-07:00","id":487919,"title":"","content":"That feels rather unintuitive to me, at least when its not completely spelled out as part of the effect. Does that mean if striking an ephemeral entity that rolled successes are still bashing as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T23:40:32-07:00","id":488015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/211700-pseshkf-question?p=487919#post487919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That feels rather unintuitive to me, at least when its not completely spelled out as part of the effect. Does that mean if striking an ephemeral entity that rolled successes are still bashing as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume so, since it only says it causes Blood Potency in lethal damage to noncorporeal entities. The successes and the weapon's damage modifier are still physical damage and therefore get downgraded to bashing as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T04:08:19-07:00","id":488124,"title":"","content":"Unless the intent was for it to be up to Blood Potency in damage, I don't think successes matter beyond determining if you hit the entity. Normally, a weapon passes though without dealing any damage. Pseshkf causes the weapon to do Blood potency in lethal damage when it hits. That is how I read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T08:54:54-07:00","id":488329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/211700-pseshkf-question?p=488124#post488124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the intent was for it to be up to Blood Potency in damage, I don't think successes matter beyond determining if you hit the entity. Normally, a weapon passes though without dealing any damage. Pseshkf causes the weapon to do Blood potency in lethal damage when it hits. That is how I read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manifested ephemerals do take damage from physical attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Physical attacks on a manifest entity that normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane. </div> </div> </div>Strix don't, if that's what you mean. Either way, the successes and the weapon's damage modifier should do what ever they would normally do to the target - lethal to a mortal, bashing to a vampire or manifested ephemeral, nothing to a Strix or unmanifested ephemeral, etc. the bonus damage (+1 to a physical target, +BP to a noncorporeal target) should always be lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}